      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I was merely stating that I requested splitting the performance settings between Public/Friends/Local last year. In addition the safety settings needs a Local. How many years has it been implemented and we still cant see the fallback shaders on our own avatars. \nSafety settings by rank is nonsense anyway. You should only ever need Public/Friends/Local. Then give individual settings per user to override or block. \nIf your team is so happy with how well the safety system currently is, then you should just go full balls and reveal the higher ranks already. Otherwise it would be wise to actually use the customisation tabs that people are familiar with to allow players to tailor the performance of the game for their hardware. For example adding Public/Friends/Local so that players have some choice between the overall visual quality compared to performance, you know like performance settings.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-08T23:13:32.723Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I don't know about everyone else but I suspect when you dreamed of Virtual Reality you wanted immersion and you wanted it to be as real as possible. This is why I rarely turn off dynamic bones and can't stand to be in avatars without them, or avatars without lip sync or eye tracking. So its strange to me that the performance settings for dynamic bones don't allow more customization filters similar to what we see in the Safety settings.\nWhat I would love to see is the ability to turn off/on dynamic bones for non-friends, friends, and yourself separately. That way you can essentially hide the non-friends much like you can using safety settings, without dulling your experience with your friends. If you must you can disable your friend's bones while keeping your own on. \nPretty please? ;)",
